386→                        <div id="content">Let $A=\{1,2,4,8,13,21,31,45,66,81,97,\ldots\}$ be the greedy Sidon sequence: we begin with $1$ and iteratively include the next smallest integer that preserves the Sidon property (i.e. there are no non-trivial solutions to $a+b=c+d$). What is the order of growth of $A$? Is it true that\[\lvert A\cap \{1,\ldots,N\}\rvert \gg N^{1/2-\epsilon}\]for all $\epsilon&#62;0$ and large $N$?</div>
387→                        <div id="problem_id"><a href="/340">#340</a>: <a href="#cite-ErGr80-340" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('ErGr80','340'); return false;">[ErGr80,p.53]</a></div>
